# What conceptlint finds in its OWN source. CI fails only if this rises.
#
# All three are the same real thing: a term declared twice, once as a P-Plan `Concept` in
# ontologies/pplan/concepts.py and once as the Python implementation in dataflow/.
#
#   Step      dataflow/step.py:23        <-> ontologies/pplan/concepts.py:40
#   Activity  dataflow/execution.py:92   <-> ontologies/pplan/concepts.py:68
#   Entity    dataflow/execution.py:78   <-> ontologies/pplan/concepts.py:81
#
# Not noise. `from conceptlint.dataflow import Step` and `from ...pplan.concepts import Step` give
# you different objects under one name — the overload this tool exists to report, reported about
# itself. That is the strongest evidence the check works.
#
# Left standing on purpose: the P-Plan correction should resolve it by making concepts.py the single
# declaration, rather than by silencing the finding. Fixing it before that lands would rename the
# same thing twice.
3
